        "hard_series": {
          "answers": {
            "hm_t1_0": "## Computing $S = \\sum_{k=1}^{1403} k^2 \\pmod{2011}$\n\n**Using the closed-form formula:**\n\n$$S = \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}, \\quad n = 1403$$\n\n$$S = \\frac{1403 \\cdot 1404 \\cdot 2807}{6}$$\n\nSince 2011 is prime, I work modulo 2011.\n\n**Reduce factors mod 2011:**\n- $1403 \\equiv 1403$\n- $1404 \\equiv 1404$\n- $2807 \\equiv 2807 - 2011 = 796$\n\n**Find $6^{-1} \\pmod{2011}$:**\nSince $6 \\cdot 335 = 2010 \\equiv -1$, we get $6^{-1} \\equiv -335 \\equiv 1676 \\pmod{2011}$.\n\n**Multiply step by step mod 2011:**\n\n$1403 \\cdot 1404 = 1{,}969{,}812$. Since $2011 \\cdot 979 = 1{,}968{,}769$, this gives $1043 \\pmod{2011}$.\n\n$1043 \\cdot 796 = 830{,}228$. Since $2011 \\cdot 412 = 828{,}532$, this gives $1696 \\pmod{2011}$.\n\n$1696 \\cdot 1676 = 2{,}842{,}496$. Since $2011 \\cdot 1413 = 2{,}841{,}543$, this gives $953 \\pmod{2011}$.\n\nANSWER: 953\n",
            "hm_t2_0": "Count of multiples of 11: ⌊89893/11⌋ = 8172\nCount of multiples of 9: ⌊89893/9⌋ = 9988\nCount of multiples of 99 (both): ⌊89893/99⌋ = 908\n\nBy inclusion-exclusion: 8172 + 9988 − 908 = 17252\n\nANSWER: 17252\n",
            "hm_t2_1": "## Solution\n\nI need to count integers $x \\in [1, 52708]$ with $\\gcd(x, 15) = 1$ and $x \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$.\n\n**Setting up the combined modulus:** Since $\\gcd(15, 7) = 1$, I work modulo $\\text{lcm}(15, 7) = 105$.\n\n**Residues mod 105 that are ≡ 2 (mod 7):**\n{2, 9, 16, 23, 30, 37, 44, 51, 58, 65, 72, 79, 86, 93, 100} — 15 values.\n\n**Remove those divisible by 3 or 5** (to ensure $\\gcd(x,15)=1$):\n- Divisible by 3: {9, 30, 51, 72, 93} — 5 values\n- Divisible by 5: {30, 65, 100} — 3 values\n- Divisible by 15: {30} — 1 value\n- Bad = 5 + 3 − 1 = 7\n\n**Valid residues:** 15 − 7 = **8** per cycle of 105, namely {2, 16, 23, 37, 44, 58, 79, 86}.\n\n**Counting full and partial cycles:**\n$$52708 = 105 \\times 501 + 103$$\n\n- Full cycles contribute: $501 \\times 8 = 4008$\n- Partial cycle (residues 1–103): all 8 valid residues (2, 16, 23, 37, 44, 58, 79, 86) are ≤ 103, contributing **8**.\n\n**Total:** $4008 + 8 = 4016$\n\nANSWER: 4016\n"
          },
